pgAdmin 4: APT repository

Supported platform matrix:

@SUPPORTED_TABLE@

@ARCHIVE_SECTION_START@
Platforms that are no longer supported. Packages for these remain available
from https://pgadmin-archive.postgresql.org/, from where they can be manually
downloaded; the archive site cannot be used as a repository.

@ARCHIVED_TABLE@
@ARCHIVE_SECTION_END@

To use this repository, run the following commands:

#
# Setup the repository
#

# Install the public key for the repository (if not done previously):
curl -fsS https://www.pgadmin.org/static/packages_pgadmin_org.pub | sudo gpg --dearmor --yes -o /etc/apt/keyrings/packages-pgadmin-org.gpg

# Create the repository configuration file. The codename is read from
# /etc/os-release, preferring UBUNTU_CODENAME, so this also works on
# Ubuntu-based distributions such as Linux Mint:
sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/pgadmin4.sources > /dev/null <<EOF
Types: deb
URIs: @BASE_URL@/apt/$(. /etc/os-release && echo ${UBUNTU_CODENAME:-$VERSION_CODENAME})
Suites: pgadmin4
Components: main
Signed-By: /etc/apt/keyrings/packages-pgadmin-org.gpg
EOF

# Remove the file created by older versions of these instructions, so the
# repository is not configured twice, then refresh the package lists:
sudo rm -f /etc/apt/sources.list.d/pgadmin4.list
sudo apt update

#
# Install pgAdmin
#

# Install for both desktop and web modes:
sudo apt install pgadmin4

# Install for desktop mode only:
sudo apt install pgadmin4-desktop

# Install for web mode only: 
sudo apt install pgadmin4-web 

# Configure the webserver, if you installed pgadmin4-web:
sudo /usr/pgadmin4/bin/setup-web.sh
